WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.135
One bartender. A line out the door that wraps around the planet.

2
00:00:04.433 --> 00:00:08.692
Everyone asks the same bartender: my job? My ex? My hair?

3
00:00:08.867 --> 00:00:11.511
The advice is good. So everyone takes it.

4
00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:14.875
Six months later, the whole town has one haircut.

5
00:00:15.067 --> 00:00:16.803
Every dog is named Biscuit.

6
00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:19.776
Every breakup text says: I've really grown.

7
00:00:21.067 --> 00:00:26.234
Real study, about stories: writers given AI ideas wrote better ones.

8
00:00:26.433 --> 00:00:27.469
And more alike.

9
00:00:29.567 --> 00:00:31.376
Which is how we lost a banana.

10
00:00:31.567 --> 00:00:35.466
The export banana was mostly one clone: the Gros Michel.

11
00:00:35.633 --> 00:00:40.275
A fungus hit, and by the 1960s that trade had collapsed.

12
00:00:41.367 --> 00:00:44.293
Its replacement, the Cavendish? Also clones.

13
00:00:44.467 --> 00:00:46.768
And a new strain of that fungus is spreading.

14
00:00:47.867 --> 00:00:51.646
Fair point, skeptics: sometimes everyone agreeing is great.

15
00:00:51.833 --> 00:00:55.882
Seatbelts. Washing hands. Nobody needs a hot take on soap.

16
00:00:56.967 --> 00:01:01.095
Full disclosure: I'm the bartender. So I'm the worst judge of this.

17
00:01:02.367 --> 00:01:06.396
When millions ask the same AI, opinions may drift closer.

18
00:01:06.567 --> 00:01:09.219
Is that a loss even when the advice is good?

19
00:01:09.400 --> 00:01:11.439
Or only when we're all wrong together?

20
00:01:14.233 --> 00:01:15.447
Here. Take a napkin.
